DEC was also a strong supporter of the ACE initiative. ACE "imploded" when
the number of alliance members (well over 100) grew so large that nobody 
could agree on anything.

 >        I do not know exactly why, but the A.C.E. never 
produce >any machine and now defunct. We are afraid that the rumour 
>(if it is true) will  produce only a similar consortium without any
>"real" result.  The user will be disappointed (again) because
>they had expected new, high performance PC standards will 
>emerge from the new consortium.

If there is any truth to the DEC/Compaq rumour, the result would not be a 
consortium--it would be a mainstream PC vendor adopting the Alpha 
architecture for its high-end products. This would add significant 
legitimacy to Alpha, which thus far has not been adopted by any 
mainstream vendors.




