In article <4737lv$1fr@alterdial.UU.NET>,  <davros@jtnet.jttechres.net> wrote:
>Hello, everyone!

> A friend of mine and I are having an argument over which company
> produces the PDP machine...I think DEC makes it.  Am I right or wrong? 

You are correct. Your friend is confused. As a matter of fact, Ken Olsen 
chose the name PDP (Programmed Data Processor) for the original PDP-1 
because the US Government would purchase "computers" only from IBM. Or so 
the legend goes.

 >Does it use Digital Unix?

Noooo--Digital UNIX is a 64-bit OS, the PDP-11 is a 16-bit architecture. 
But the original "Son of Multics" Unix was developed on a PDP-7.

By the way, a US company called Mentec now has responsibility for all 
PDP-11 hardware and software. DEC divested the PDP line about a year ago.


