	VXT systems can load their software either from a host system (if the
terminal has 10 meg of memory or more) or from an InfoServer.  The server
based software is on CD (the InfoServer's supported load medium.) Last I knew,
when you order the VXT software, you get 1 host set (in the medium of your
choice for the OS of your choice) and the server CD.  The general part number
is QA-XNGA*-** (where the '8' vary by OS and media type.)  The current version
of the VXT software is V2.1.

