In article <4737lv$1fr@alterdial.UU.NET>, davros@jtnet.jttechres.net writes:
>Hello, everyone!
>	A friend of mine and I are having an argument over which company 
> produces the PDP machine...I think DEC makes it.  Am I right or wrong?  
> Does it use Digital Unix?
>
>	Please reply to davros@jttechres.net
>

Which PDP?  PDP 1, 6, 8, 10, and others are no longer made.  DEC sold the
rights to the PDP-11 and it's RSX operating system, but still operates the
manufacturing plant.

PDP-11 supports a whole collection of operating systems, including RSX-11M,
RSX-11M+ (and other RSX-11 variants), RT-11, RSTS, UV711M (a UNIX), and old
copies of BSD UNIX (maybe new copies, I'm not sure).

Digital UNIX (formerly OSF/1) is a 64 bit UNIX and does not run on the 16 bit
PDP-11.

