In article <46k6iiINNp42@oak.cis.ohio-state.edu>, 
block@cis.ohio-state.edu (brad block) writes...
> How do I switch my network device from 10base5 (AUI) to 10baseT on
> an Alphastation?  it seems to want to auto select AUI at boot time
> but we have UTP here.

    At the Console >>> prompt, type

    	>>> set ewa0_mode AUI           ! for thinwire

    	>>> set ewa0_mode Twisted-Pair  ! for twisted pair

    These selections work for both the embedded Ethernet controller (on
    Alphastation models 200 and 250) and for the DE435 PCI-Ethernet add-in
    card used on the Alphastation 400.  The thickwire port on the
    DE435 can be accessed by selecting AUI and moving a jumper plug on the
    board.

    Note that the port designator "a" in "ewa0" increments through the
    alphabet for additional Ethernet ports (ewb0, ewc0, ...).

    Autoselection has had a checkered history with this controller, and I
    would avoid it when possible.

