We have a lab of DEC Decstation 425c PC compatable machines onto which
we are trying to load pathworks, and have been since Mid August.  It
seems that these machines are incompatable with emm386.  We have tried
versions from dos 5.0, dos 6.22, and the ones that come with windows and
lanman 2.2c.  In all cases, if we have emm386 loaded, ethernet software
will not load.  We have even tried excluding all of the upper memory
(x=b000-efff).  Nothing works.  Digital technical support is terrible.
They will call, confirm there is a problem, and then never call back
with solutions.  We can configure the same set up to work on Gateway
machines.  No problems on the gateways, they work like a charm out of
the box.  But on the 425c, no luck - Pathworks won't work; msclient
won't work, lanman 2.2c won't work.  

Because we have tried to get Digital (the company that is saying that it
can be a corporate support solution) to help, and they won't, I am
turning to the net.  Does anyone have a Digital 425c working in a tcp/ip
networking environment?  If so, could you send me the secret?

By the way, we have tried Digital Etherworks 3, DEPCA and 3Com Etherlink
3 boards in the 425c, and all fail in the same fashion.  The 3Com board
doesn't even use any upper memory, so it isn't likely that it is a
memory problem with the ethernet board.

One additional piece of information, when they fail, they always say
that they cannot read from drive c.

Here's hoping that someone else got one of these machines and that we
can get some idea what is causing the problems.

Jim




