In article <1995Oct24.190031.1@spcvxb.spc.edu>, terry@spcvxb.spc.edu� says...
>  The VMS driver seems to be quite happy with 2048 byte sectors on CD's.
>However, the ROM bootstrap doesn't like 'em - try booting a VMS distrib-
>ution CD. I know the CDU-561 can deal with this transparently, perhaps
>some versions of the 541 can as well. I've tried NEC and Toshiba drives
>and they've all failed to boot, but work Ok on a running system.
>

The OpenVMS driver first does a sense mode SCSI command.  If the block size is 
not already 512Kb, then it send a set mode command to set the block size to 
512kb.

OpenVMS and (I think, Digital Unix) cannot use CD-ROM drives which implement 
only 2K block size.  But, maybe one day, we will finally get this fixed.


