According to the 2100/3100 manual I have, it's the "Mouse & Keyboard"
test. Make sure that the cables for the mouse & keyboard are plugged
in properly. If they are, try getting your hands on another mouse and
DEC keyboard and try those out.

> Background:  This machine is in my 'lab' at a university-operated used
> computer store.  I'd like to get this on the shelf so it can bring in some
> money, but I'm at a loss.  First off, what OS is native to a DS 3100, does
> this sound like a hardware or software problem, and are the memory sims and
> dsim compatible with any non-Dec product? (Any variety of MS-Dos clone,
> Macintosh, Amiga or Sun)  Is the beautiful 20-in monitor (with standard DEC
> cable, something like 15-pin on the CPU side and separated RGB cables with
> keyboard and mouse imputs on a box near the monitor termination) compatible
> in any way with any of the above systems, and if so, what additional cords
> or connectors are called for?  Finally, is there a blue book used price for
> this hardware?

The DS3100 runs Ultrix 4.x. The SIMMs aren't compatible with anything
else, except maybe DS5000/1x0 and DS5000/xx machines.

The monitor sounds like a VR299 (rounded 20" screen). If it's a
cylindrical curved screen (Sony Trinitron tube) at 20" you can't run it on
the DS3100 - it needs a PMAGB-x card in machine with TurboChannel slots
(which the DS3100 doesn't have.) If it's actually a 17" Trinitron,
then you've got a really nice monitor.
