In article <30858902.41C6@yalph2.physics.yale.edu>, Weiwen Liu 
<liu@yalph2.physics.yale.edu> writes:

|>I got the patch for SCSI driver on VMS5.5, but I do not know the format
|>of this file.
|>Could someone tell me how to install the patch ftp'd from
|>ftp.service.digital.com?

You don't say which patch it is, but I'll guess it's VAXSCSI03_061.  I can
understand your confusion - the cover letter doesn't tell you all you need to
know (you DID read the cover letter, didn't you?  It's at:

  ftp://ftp.service.digital.com/public/vms/vax/v6.1/vaxscsi03_061.README

(I found this through the search utility at the patch server's page at:

  http://www.service.digital.com/html/patch_public.html

Anyway, the patch itself is supplied as five files with names of the form:

  VAXSCSI03_061.A-DCX_VAXEXE

Each of these files is a self-expanding compressed image file. RUN each file
to expand them to files with names like VAXSCSI03_061.A.  When you have
expanded all five files, use VMSINSTAL to install the patch as instructed in
the cover letter.

Most of the patches from this server are compressed in this manner.
