In article <46jo9c$icm@ixnews3.ix.netcom.com>, treahy@ix.netcom.com (Barry Treahy) writes:
[story deleted]
> Though I am curious why, I much more interested in just getting this
> fixed.  

  DEC usually sets the SCSI host adapter ID in their systems to 6. This was to
support dual-host SCSI configurations (the second CPU would be ID 7, so that
inter-CPU messages would have priority). This support was never added, except
recently on a limited number of new AXP systems. You should be able to change
the host's ID with a SET SCSI command at the >>> prompt.

  Another problem you may run into is that the BA350 has an internal cable
length equivalent of a bazillion feet (actually, 3.3, which is a good part of
the total allowable length for a fast SCSI chain). "Fortunately", most native
DEC SCSI adapters aren't fast SCSI, so you get twice the distance at half the
speed...

