<haag@me.lsu.edu> wrote:

>Hello all!
>
>I've just been told that there may be some problems with 
>overheating when putting a 7200 rpm RZ29 (4.3 GB) SCSI drive 
>into the cabinet of an Alpha workstation (in particular, a 
>3000 model 400). I am told that the 5400 rpm is recommended...
>Can anyone corroborate this? 
>
>I'd prefer responses by Email.
>
    I believe the two reasons DEC offers this drive _only_ as a -VA
(StorageWorks carrier) model is because of ventilaion and power-up
current draw concerns. This cannot be fixed on a BA-353, but the BA-350
has been upgraded (and can be user-upgarded) with redundant fans and a
heftier power supply. The new BA-36x's evidently are also so equiped.

    You might consider one of these external carriers if you have the $,
since it would allow you to use the 3000-400's second (external) SCSI bus
as well.
                  
