In article <Your_address.8.0014D010@mindlink.net>,
    Your_address@mindlink.net (Herb Peters) writes:

> I have a VAX 6610 clustered with a VAX 4100, both running VMS 5.5-2 on 
> separate system disks. The 6610 has a KFMSA DSSI adapter card to which two MTI 
> DSSI disks are attached. The 4100 has an embedded DSSI controller to which 3 
> DEC DSSI disks are attached. At this time these computers are clustered via 
> ETHERNET.

> Both computers have the same allocation class and the 5 disks involved have 
> different unit numbers. If I poweroff my cluster and physically connect the 
> two DSSI busses and reboot will both computers automatically detect the new 
> connection path and use it, or is some cluster  reconfiguation necessary?

Should work.  Check to see that SYS$SYSTEM:MODPARAMS.DAT has the line
	INTERCONNECT="NICI"
on each system.  I think the presence of DSSI bus requires this even in
single-hosted configurations, but if the value is "NI" change it to "NICI"
and perform an autogen.

Make sure the DSSI addresses of each node are different.  Default is 7. Change
one to 6.

