Alan Lo (loa@rastro.Colorado.EDU) wrote:
: I have a DEC 3000/600M with a ZLX-E1 graphics card and a Digital
: VRC16 color monitor. I recently acquired a large 22" Ardent Computer
: monitor as a freebie. Upon connecting it to my DEC, the larger
: screen does not appear to sync correctly. Both monitors use only
: the RGB coaxials, and do not use the H and V sync lines.
: Unfortunately, I have no documentation for this Ardent monitor
: other than the label on the back, which says 110-120V, 50-60Hz
: Sony Trinitron graphic display monitor.

The ZLX-E1 card decides whether to put sync on green based on the
setting of one of the EEPROM variables.  Be sure to do

	>>> set tga_sync_green 1
	>>> init

First.  The dip switches on the back of the ZLX card will provide a
variety of resolutions/sync-rates to try.

-Ron




