X-Deja-AN: 118034175
references: <466e2q$3gkj@te6000.otc.lsu.edu> <1995Oct20.104137@axp2.umkc.edu>
organization: USG
reply-to: ftw@zk3.dec.com
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

The RZ29's do require extra cooling.  I don't recall that these drives
have been qualified IN the DEC3000 model 400 (aka Sandpiper.)  They
almost certainly will work WITH the model 400 provided they're mounted
in an appropriate StorageWorks box.

The model 400 uses 53C94's for the SCSI interfaces.  If you need the
storage of the 29 that's one thing but you may be throwing away a bit
of performance.  The 53C94's provide a "slow/narrow" bus which means
a max. throughput of 5MB/s in theory.  If you're going to get RZ29's
for that machine I'd suggest buying a dual SCSI adaptor (the PMAZC)
to go with it.  This provides two narrow/fast buses each capable of
10MB/s.

