Currently you are unable to run a large screen fixed scan monitor on 
your PC since the computer video board generates several scan rates 
and the fixed scan monitor can only display one (not multi-scan 
monitor).  Several big screen fixed scan monitors from mainframes,
MAC systems, SUN's, etc. are sitting in storerooms collecting dust.
Many of these monitors are capable of 1280 X 1024 and have great
resolution.  After some initial investigation you'll find most have
SONY engines (trinitron tubes)!!!

YOU CAN RUN THESE MONITORS ON YOUR PC!!!!!!

BEHR Micro-Electronics Inc. has developed a small controller which 
interfaces between your computer and monitor(s) to control where the VGA 
signal is sent and how.  The unit has two L.E.D.'s on the front to 
indicate which mode it is in (HI-SCAN or MULTI-SCAN).  Initially the unit 
must be set up for your particular monitor (selection of horizontal and 
vertical lock frequencies) this programs the controller to switch the VGA 
signal to the fixed scan monitor when the horizontal and vertical sync 
signals are appropriate.  Unless both horizontal and vertical sync 
signals are those selected when you setup the unit the VGA signals are 
sent to the Multi-scan output.  The unit has three VGA connectors on the 
back, one connects to your computer VGA board output.  This is the video 
input to the controller.  Dependant on the scan rate generated by the PC, 
the VVC-10 controller switches this video, sync, etc to the appropriate 
output (MULTI-SCAN or HI-SCAN) monitor.

You do not NEED to run a multi-scan monitor besides your fixed scan 
monitor.  For instance if your autoexec.bat brings you right into
Windows at 1280 X 1024 resolution you simply will see nothing on the
big screen before the VVC-10 detects the HI-SCAN mode, and switches the
video over to it.

The unit has sync polarity detection/correction and normally ships sync 
negative, if required (special order) the output for the HI-SCAN mode can 
be set for sync positive (very few monitors require positive sync).  This
is extremely important, since some monitors can be permanently damaged by
operating them with the wrong sync signals!

The unit allows for individual horizontal and vertical sync OR, composite 
sync, OR sync-on-green.  These selections are all user configurable by
internal jumper selection.

If the blanking of the big screen monitor prevents you from viewing the 
image on the left side of the screen the unit has the ability to shift 
horizontal position (horizontal phase compensation).  This is accomplished
by changing jumpers and adjusting an internal potentiometer to center 
the image on the CRT.  All adjustments and configuration information is
included with the unit.

The unit is 7" wide X 5-1/4" deep X 1-1/2" high, exterior PC-bone color 
with grey faceplate.  An external power adapter (120 VAC) is included.
Alternate power sources (220 VAC) can be adapted to power the unit 

The unit sells for $ 330.00, $ 25.00 shipping and handling, and 7% Goods
and Services Tax (Canadian dollars).  Optional cables are also available.

