In article <465bfa$p3t@rs18.hrz.th-darmstadt.de> richard@mailhost.isa.informatik.th-darmstadt.de (Richard Froehning) wrote:
> There is currently a JENSEN-Firmware (1.9) and an ARC-console installed,
> and I want to make a firmware-update to 3.3 but the JENSEN-Firmware will
> only accept JNUPDATE.EXE and .BIN. If this doesn't matter, how am I 
> supposed to install a SRM console on the AlphaPC? Im reading FAQ's and
> News, but I never get a hint to this task.


Richard,

The DECpc AXP150 FlashRAM actually contains both ARC and SRM Consoles 
as default. To switch to the SRM Console on a DECpc AXP150 do the following:

From the ARC Console Boot Menu, Select 'Supplementary menu...' 
Then 'Set up the system...'. 
Now goto 'Switch to OpenVMS or OSF Console...'
Choose either OpenVMS or OSF Console. Hit return a couple of times
        then power cycle the system. It is now in the SRM Console.

To get back to the ARC Console from the SRM Console, type 'SET OS NT' 
then power cycle the system.

"Firmware-update to 3.3", I assume, is Version 3.3 of the CDROM. This 
disk actually has V1.9 of the firmware, the version you are running.
The update proceedure is described in the Release Notes/Instructions
which accompany the CDROM. Basically, you boot the CDROM from the SRM
Console, and type in the location of the relevant firmware on the disk.

Hope this helps explain things a bit...


Gordon


