> while using NETSCAPE, my DECWINDOWS session crashes

I used to have hangs when running an app on a Sun.  It takes the mouse,
hangs before it gives it back.  Bet if you log on and kill netscape, it 
comes back.  Sometimes it hung, sometimes it crashed.  I also had that.
Programmer *assumed* I had a 64K buffer, instead of asking (against
X11 protocol!).  Got an alpha, it has 64K buffer, so I probably won't
see it happen now.  Crash or hang just depends on the state, it seems.

I did get feedback from someone stating that killing Netscape indeeds
frees up his workstation.  So it appears Netscape also doesn't follow
the X11 protocol, to ask the workstation what size buffer it can 
handle, and just assumes it's 64K.  I haven't proven that is the case,
but it sure sounds like it. 

