  This might be a great time to consider implementing DCE.  DCE is 
considered a very viable alternative to NIS and it's variants..ONC+.
DCE is supported and provided by Digital, SGI, HP, IBM, many others.
you can also get PC, Windows NT and Windows 95 DCE products from
Digital and other vendors.

   Using DCE you could use replicated services to build some back-up
redundancy into your configuration.  There are also some excellent DCE
manager products available to help manage DCE (some are thrown in as
extras, such as the DCE Director on Digital's DCE for Windows NT 
product.)

   There are a number of applications for CASE and OO based development
that you can use on top of DCE, or you can use DCE as your development
environment instead of developing applications to support multiple 
hardware/OS platforms, if that is your use of these computers.

   The cost of moving to DCE is minimal, the DCE Runtimes are bundled
into all the OS's these days (not sure about SGI).

