>I'm searching for a newer eprom binary image from the EMULEX UC04 Q bus
>SCSI controller. I have an old "Applicon Workstation" with an uVAX II
>cpu an try to install NetBSD. The currently firmware on the controller
>hungs while the initialization from the NetBSD driver.

A while back on the port-vax mailing list, it was mentioned that
there have been a few modifications made to the mscp driver.  In particular,
the driver was polling the controller so quickly at one point in
initialization that the microprocessor on the controller spent 100%
of its time responding to the polls, and none of its time completing
the initialization.  This is supposedly fixed in the very latest
release of the vax port.

>I have mailed to tech-support@europe.emulex.com an got no answer jet :-(

At least in the U.S., Emulex has sold most (or all) of its Q-bus or
Unibus lines to other companies, who now do the support.  The people
