In article <45dprs$c9q@explorer.csc.com>, rmsmith@csc.com (Robert Smith) writes:
|>Help please
|>I have looked thru the archives on line at sunsite, wizvax, etc.
|>I have not been able to find out what all the jumpers are for on
|>the RQDX3 board.
|>
|>I assume that the jumpers on the bottom (just above the last
|>set of DC005 chips) is the address setting.  These are just 
|>below the DC7006 chip and are un labelled on all of my boards.
|>

That is correct, with the fingers pointing down the right most jumper
(near the center of the board is address bit 2, the left most jumper is 
(near the board edge is address bit 11. The normal address for this module
is 17772150, but this is only when one MSCP device is in the backplane. If
more than one device is installed then one of them must be changed to a
location in the floating address space.

|>On the left edge (fingers down) of the board there are 4 jumpers.
|>There actuall looks like there should be 5 but there are 4, they
|>line up with pins 3 and 4 of the 21-17311-01 chip.

The jumpers set the starting Logical Unit Number of the drives. The 
factory configuration is to have no jumpers 
installed.

|>
|>There are 4 more jumper pairs above the 21-17311 chip (two pair
|>next to a resister pack (sip)

These two jumpers are also used to set the starting LUN of the drives.
The factory configuration is to have no jumpers installed.

|> and two pair a little above that 
|>and next to another resister pack).

This set of four pins in a single row are labelled with pin 1 towards 
the module fingers and pin 4 towards the module handle. The factory
configuration is to have a jumper between positions 1 and 2 which is the
standard configuration for installation in a BA23 box (the tall, narrow 
MicroPDP-11 and MicroVAX box.) This configuration places the HEADSEL3_L and 
REDUCWRTI_L signals on the same connector pin. A jumper between positions
2 and 3 places these signals on separate connector pins and I believe is the
configuration for a BA123 or BA200 box, but my manual is a unclear on this and
it's been 10 years since I did this design so my brain is unclear also.

>
