In article <Pine.3.89.9510102211.A10089-0100000@corn.cso.niu.edu> z931205@corn.cso.niu.edu (David Kim) writes:
>From: z931205@corn.cso.niu.edu (David Kim)
>Subject: What is ECC RAM?
>Date: 10 Oct 1995 23:00:51 -0500

>In the October issue of Computer Graphics World under the Spotlight column in
>the article: "Digital Delivers Dynamite Workstations" they mention...

>The Model 600 5/266 is priced at $31,800 and includes 32MB of ECC RAM...

>My question is:  What kind of memory is ECC RAM?

>If you know, please post an answer here or e-mail me one...Thanks!

>Dave
>z931205@corn.cso.niu.edu


ECC

Error Checking and Correcting (ECC). All bits transferred go to a buffer are 
checked and corrected.  With this architecture, only minimal delay is 
encountered ffor the first bits accessed and no delay for subsequent bits.

ECC provides for improved reliability of both hard and soft fails


