: Is there a "32-bit" mode or some similar feature for the cxx
: C++ compiler. I would like to ensure that all pointers fit
: within 4 bytes instead of the 8 usually required on the alpha.

In C++ v5.0 and above the -taso switch will ensure running in the lower
address half, along with using the -xtaso switch & pragmas for using
32-bit pointers. Read the man pages & bookreader docs for 5.0 and above
for more specific information.

Also, not converting the code to be 64-bit clean is just prolonging the
inevitable. I'd recommend biting the bullet now if possible.
