efricha@tigger.cs.Colorado.EDU (Eric F. Richards) writes:

> 	If so, does anyone have any strong preferences
> for what brand of disk to go with (or avoid)?  

I have had exceptionally good experiences with Seagate Barracuda 2
drives on VAX & Alpha systems.  They come in 2 & 4 Gb capacities,
have lightning fast response, are quiet, and are reasonably well priced.

I started buying these during the transition from Digital->Quantum
drives, when the market was in chaos and everyone had a different story
about what was available from whom.  Because the Barracudas are faster
than the 2Gb Quantums (DSP 3210), I've continued to buy Barracudas. 

The 32550N is what I've been buying; that's N for Narrow.  Don't get
rooked by someone selling a Hawk as a Barracuda 2; the part number
will be different.

