  Rooked? The Hawk 4 (ST15230N) has an average seek time 0.5 ms longer
than the Barracuda 4 (ST15150N), the same cpapcity (though half as big a
cache, 0.5 Mbyte vs. 1 Mbyte), runs much cooler than a Barracuda 4 (which
Digital says _not_ put in a BA353, that's one of the reasons they just
came out with the BA 36x's), and uses less power to spin up. And oh, yes,
the street prices for Hawk 4's are generally $200 less than for the less
reliable 'cudas (~$1080 for a bare drives vs. ~$1280).

    We have lots of Hawk 4's (~18) and have yet to have a problem with any
of them. The only drawback I can see for your application is that the
Barracuda 4 --- if it doesn't overheat --- will give better performance
for swapping operations under unix, because of the larger cache size.
