Indeed.  And, to those others who collect such systems. please
carefully preserve them by keeping them in good running condition
whenever possible.  At the very least:

- if you can, duplicate EPROMs, etc. 
- make sure that you keep safe backup copies of all software, 
- test the power supplies before powering systems up that haven't been 
  used in quite a while,
- repair boards by troubleshooting them and replacing the failed
  components (as opposed to board swapping)
- carefully inspect any system that has been moved for any loose 
  parts, wires, etc. that could short something out, etc.

