(Eric Jolley) writes:
>I recently purchased a DEC Starion 800i (Pentium 100, 1gig HD and CDROM)
>and I'd like to add a tape backup drive, preferably IDE.
>
>My question is this: how do I add an IDE device to my Starion?  There
>doesn't seem to be any free plugs on the motherboard, with the floppy,
>CD-ROM, and Hard Drive plugged in, so can IDE be daisy chained? (Sorry if
>these questions are newbiesque) I'm frustrated over the lack of decent
>technical information about this machine.  The manual is zero help about
>adding IDE drives.  I'd also like to know if the Starion has an IDE or
>EIDE interface (is there a way to check) as well as whether the card slots
>are ISA or EISA (what's the difference). 

I believe that this model has only a single IDE controller - you would need
to add a separate EIDE controller (they're cheap).  The slots are ISA
(and PCI).

Note that there's only one IDE tape drive I know of, a Conner of limited
capacity and high price.  I was expecting to see a bunch of such released
about now (I'd like one myself), but nothing yet.

You can call Starion PC support with questions such as yours.  The number is
on your warranty card (I don't have it handy).

