I hope this is an appropriate forum for my line of question:

I have a client at our site running a Digital desktop pc (model: LPx+ 
486DX2 ver 1.02) with 32MB Ram and a 1 gig HD, with an Adaptec SCSI bios 
(AHA  -1540CF/1542CF bio version 2.01)/NEC 5FG monitor, with Matrox video 
card.  The pc is running within a MS Windows 3.11 Workgroup network, and 
primarily used for graphics. When running Adobe PHotoshop (for Windows), 
and opening up a 5-10MB image, the system becomes brutally slow (ie when 
dragging across a window, it takes about four seconds for it to show up 
at the new location on the screen, among other things). Everything looks 
fine as far as what Photoshop requires; ie 32mb ram/100mb swapdisk for 
windows/hd is regularly defragmented/300mb free space on the hd.  

My next line of action is to setup a partition on the hd, so that 
