Of course you all remember the wonderful DEC 433 Workstation?
(A pizza-box 486, with built-in SCSI, Ethernet, and a TIGA
video display system which can put normal DOS text mode onto
a 1280x1024 fixed-frequency display.)

(Of course, if you *DO* remember it, you are several steps
ahead of DEC, which seems to have forgotten that it ever sold
such a thing.  How quickly time passes ...)

Does anyone know whether this system will work with Windows 95?
Or any form of Intel-based Unix, such as NEXTSTEP or Linux?
Or if there is a workable X-Windows server?

The common thread in this question concerns the support for the
TIGA video display system available in any such software.  Does
anyone know how best to encourage DEC to provide on-going
support for a computer which they sold so recently?

