>recognised for what it was, but when I tried to format the disk using the card,
>I received:
>  SCSI command failure <blah>
>  Sense key - device not ready <blah>

	RZ drives only spinup after receiving a SCSI spinup command. This
is to keep the powersupply going if you have large numbers of them on a
single power rail.

>I seem to recall hearing somewhere that DEC VAX SCSI devices are not really
>using SCSI protocols, and have been lobotomised to their own proprietry

	Nonsense. The only thing that has to be done is set (or reset?) a
specific bit in one of the mode pages of the drive. Look for a program
MODE8.EXE (runs on a PC with ASPI scsi drivers).

Maybe it's on gatekeeper.dec.com

Wilko



