Neil Tancock <Neil_Tancock@npgtq02.pai01.nt.com> wrote:
>Which do you think is the better machine?  I have two suppliers both 
>saying that their particular selection is best on price and performance.  
>Anyone got any ideas out there?  
>
>Many fanx,
>
>Neil
>
>
Its really not a case of better or worse.  Its really a case for speed and 
expandability!  Also you are not comparing apples to apples.  A 2000 5/250 will run 
at just about the same speed as a 2100 5/250.  The 5/250, cpu to cpu will out 
perform a 4/275.  See the web page for the latest performance numbers 
http://www.digital.com.

The real difference is in expandability, the 2000 is 1-2 cpu's while the 2100 is 1-4 
cpu's.  The 2100 can go to 2 GB memory (with 3 cpus, 1GB with 4) while the 2000 is 
1GB.  Finally there is more room in the 2100 pedestal for storageworks devices (16) 
while the 2000 is 7. (there may be a small difference in the number of slots too)

Bottom line, the 2100 buys you more expandability...

Hope this helps...

Jeff






