DEC SCSI disks, and DEC OSs, use full SCSI protocols these days. The 
VS2000 series had (as I have heard) a partial SCSI implementation. Anything
more recent is standard. Different manufacturers do read the standard
differently though, and there are jumper options on disk drives that may
need to be set differently for different controllers.




