In article <440026635wnr@logitek.demon.co.uk>, Matt Walsmsley <mattw@logitek.demon.co.uk> writes:
>The title says it all

not really

>, anybody got any recommendations ?
>
>

Start with BACKUP.  That will be sufficient if you can be down
for a day or so while you restore image backups of your disks onto a new 
(or repaired) system.  If you're only worried about losing a disk now
and then, you can set everything up to be present on duplicate disks.

If you can't be down for the time it takes to restore from backups, then you
need to avoid the disaster in the first place, for instance by setting up a
WAN based cluster with duplicate disks at each site, so that that hurricane
or whatever only wipes out part of your system and the rest can carry on. 

Regards,

