This reply was mailed by a co-worker in response to the original question,
but just in case anyone else was wondering the same things, I'm posting it
here as well.

> (i) Does anyone know whether this a separate software product, and if so,
> what is the DEC order number?  The local DEC office here does not appear
> to know much about the FullVideo Supreme (except the price!), let alone
> software support for the product. 

        Yes, "Digital Light & Sound Pack" is a separate software
        product, which will be bundled (as a CD) with all AlphaStation
        systems.  If you already have an AlphaStation system and would
        like to order it separtely here is the part number and
        information:

        Part #:  QB-4LTAA-SA    License & CD-ROM Pack   $ 25.00
                                Includes: 
                                        Single-user License
                                        Media
                                        Documentation

> (ii) What is included in the "Digital Light & Sound Pack"?  We need to 
> capture images and process them in (nearly) real time - does the Pack 
> including a programming interface that can be accessed via Visual C++?

        You get the software support fot the FullVideo Supreme,
        FullVideo Supreme JPEG, Software JPEG Codec and an MPEG-1
        video player. 

        The programming interface you use would be the "Video For
        Windows" interface which is part of Windows NT.  You might
        have to buy the Window NT SDK to get that support.  

        For video capture, you would use the "AVIcap" interface.


