It depends on how far you want to expand the system in the future.  I
personally like the 2100 better because it can be expanded to 1Gb of
RAM with 4 CPUs (2Gb with 3 CPUs) and have two full storage works
shelves.  The only limitation I don't like is only having three PCI
slots, hopefully they'll come out with a new 2100 that will have 8 PCI
slots and only three EISA slots.  

